# The local production-shaped stack's own env file (#76/#246's local-testing complement —
# NOT the real cloud deployment #246 tracks itself, which is a k3s-on-Hetzner + managed-Postgres
# cluster per ADR-049, still start-gated on Musti's architecture call for #246 specifically).
# Copy to `.env` at the repo root, then:
#
#   docker compose -f docker-compose.yml -f docker-compose.prod.yml up --build
#
# Frontend on http://localhost:8080, API on http://localhost:3000 — the exact ports the
# stakeholder's own local test used.
#
# WHY THIS FILE IS THE ONE PLACE THESE TWO VALUES LIVE: API_ORIGIN and WEB_ORIGIN are each
# set ONCE below and docker-compose.prod.yml flows them into BOTH sides — the API's
# CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS/WEB_APP_URL/BETTER_AUTH_URL AND the web image's build-time
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL — never hand-duplicated across two files that can silently drift
# apart. A mismatch between "what origin the browser is actually on" and "what origin the
# API/web bundle were told to expect" is the exact, single root cause behind all four
# symptoms the stakeholder saw (guest browsing, registration, login, the QR code all failing
# identically) — see e2e/harness/README.md's own documented note on `expo export --clear`
# for the specific stale-bundle shape of that class of bug.
API_PORT=3000
WEB_PORT=8080
API_ORIGIN=http://localhost:3000
WEB_ORIGIN=http://localhost:8080

# Postgres — synthetic local credentials, matching docker-compose.yml's own base stack
# (never real values, ADR-0003 §4.2).
POSTGRES_USER=steuereule
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=steuereule
POSTGRES_DB=steuereule

# NODE_ENV=production (set in docker-compose.prod.yml) makes the API refuse to boot with a
# guessable default for any secret below — every resolve*(env) function in
# apps/api/src/{auth,prisma}/*.ts throws instead (ADR-0008/ADR-0012, "a control that proves
# itself by refusing to start" rather than silently running unencrypted/unsigned). The
# values below are synthetic, fine for a `localhost` test stack; generate real ones
# (`npx cloak generate` for the encryption key, a long random string for the two secrets)
# before pointing this compose file at anything beyond your own machine.
GUEST_SESSION_SECRET=local-prod-test-guest-session-secret-change-me
PRISMA_FIELD_ENCRYPTION_KEY=k1.aesgcm256.MDEyMzQ1Njc4OWFiY2RlZjAxMjM0NTY3ODlhYmNkZWY=
BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=local-prod-test-better-auth-secret-change-me-0123456789

# Google OAuth (REQ-008) — the SAME dev-only placeholder better-auth already accepts on
# every non-production run in this repo (apps/api/src/auth/better-auth.ts's own
# DEV_ONLY_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID/SECRET), set explicitly here because NODE_ENV=production turns
# off that automatic fallback (resolveGoogleClientId only refuses to *invent* a value under
# NODE_ENV=production — it still accepts one handed to it explicitly, at any NODE_ENV).
# This makes the button render and its plumbing provable; it is NOT a real Google OAuth
# handshake — that needs real console.cloud.google.com credentials (#170, still open).
# Swap for real values before pointing this compose file at anything beyond your own
# machine.
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=dev-only-google-client-id
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=dev-only-google-client-secret
